  data: {
    LLM: 'Deal: First dealer random; dealer gives 4 cards to player on right and 4 face down on table. That player bids 9–13 (capture value) if possible, then must create a house of that value, pick up cards of that value, or throw the bid card as loose. Dealer then deals remainder in fours counter-clockwise (bidder has 11 cards, others 12). Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: play one card to (1) create or add to a house, (2) pick up matching cards or houses, or (3) throw a loose card. Houses are piles of 9–13 capture value; ordinary houses can be broken or cemented; cemented houses cannot be broken. Must pick up all cards that match the played card. Sweep (taking all floor cards) scores 50 (25 on first play, 0 on last). Last picker takes any remaining loose cards.',
    Player: 'Deal: First dealer random; dealer gives 4 cards to player on right and 4 face down on table. That player bids 9–13 (capture value) if possible, then must create a house of that value, pick up cards of that value, or throw the bid card as loose. Dealer then deals remainder in fours counter-clockwise (bidder has 11 cards, others 12). Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: play one card to (1) create or add to a house, (2) pick up matching cards or houses, or (3) throw a loose card. Houses are piles of 9–13 capture value; ordinary houses can be broken or cemented; cemented houses cannot be broken. Must pick up all cards that match the played card. Sweep (taking all floor cards) scores 50 (25 on first play, 0 on last). Last picker takes any remaining loose cards.',
    objective: 'Capture cards worth points from the layout (floor). The game ends when one team has a lead of at least 100 points over the other (a baazi). Capture by playing a card that matches the capture value of one or more cards or houses on the table; build houses (piles that can only be captured as a unit) to protect or consolidate captures.',
    gameplay: 'Deal: First dealer random; dealer gives 4 cards to player on right and 4 face down on table. That player bids 9–13 (capture value) if possible, then must create a house of that value, pick up cards of that value, or throw the bid card as loose. Dealer then deals remainder in fours counter-clockwise (bidder has 11 cards, others 12). Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: play one card to (1) create or add to a house, (2) pick up matching cards or houses, or (3) throw a loose card. Houses are piles of 9–13 capture value; ordinary houses can be broken or cemented; cemented houses cannot be broken. Must pick up all cards that match the played card. Sweep (taking all floor cards) scores 50 (25 on first play, 0 on last). Last picker takes any remaining loose cards.',
    keyRules: [
      'Capture value: A=1, 2–10 face, J=11, Q=12, K=13',
      'Only spades (1–13), aces of other suits (1 each), and 10♦ (6) score; total 100 points',
      'First team to lead by 100 wins one baazi; team scoring under 9 in a deal loses a baazi immediately',
      'House owner must hold a card matching house value until captured or broken',
    ],
