    turnFlow: 'Deal: First dealer random; dealer gives 4 cards to player on right and 4 face down on table. That player bids 9–13 (capture value) if possible, then must create a house of that value, pick up cards of that value, or throw the bid card as loose. Dealer then deals remainder in fours counter-clockwise (bidder has 11 cards, others 12). Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: play one card to (1) create or add to a house, (2) pick up matching cards or houses, or (3) throw a loose card. Houses are piles of 9–13 capture value; ordinary houses can be broken or cemented; cemented houses cannot be broken. Must pick up all cards that match the played card. Sweep (taking all floor cards) scores 50 (25 on first play, 0 on last). Last picker takes any remaining loose cards.',
