    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Capture cards worth points from the layout (floor). The game ends when one team has a lead of at least 100 points over the other (a baazi). Capture by playing a card that matches the capture value of one or more cards or houses on the table; build houses (piles that can only be captured as a unit) to protect or consolidate captures.',
      'Turn-flow example: Deal: First dealer random; dealer gives 4 cards to player on right and 4 face down on table. That player bids 9–13 (capture value) if possible, then must create a house of that value, pick up cards of that value, or throw the bid card as loose. Dealer then deals remainder in fours counter-clockwise (bidder has 11 cards, others 12). Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: play one card to (1) create or add to a house, (2) pick up matching cards or houses, or (3) throw a loose card. Houses are piles of 9–13 capture value; ordinary houses can be broken or cemented; cemented houses cannot be broken. Must pick up all cards that match the played card. Sweep (taking all floor cards) scores 50 (25 on first play, 0 on last). Last picker takes any remaining loose cards.',
      'Scoring example: Spades 1–13 points (K=13 down to A=1), aces of other suits 1 each, 10♦ = 6; total 100. Sweep: 50 (25 on first play, 0 on last). First team to lead by 100 wins one baazi. Team scoring under 9 in a deal loses a baazi. First team to achieve a lead of 100 or more points over the other team wins one baazi. Team scoring fewer than 9 points in a deal loses a baazi immediately..',
